<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!--
        The Strata Wedge in black and white: point right, concave back
        edge, cut into five bands of rock, white on the launcher's #0A0A0A
        ground. Bands one, three and five are solid white; two and four are
        62% white, the rhythm the mark has wherever it is monochrome (the
        app's own StrataWedge, the loaders, ic_notification).

        One drawable, three jobs: the launcher icon's foreground, its themed
        (monochrome) layer, and the system splash's icon. The splash hands
        over to the app's own drawing of this mark, so the icon you tap, the
        splash and the first frame of the app all show the same thing.

        The bands are separated, not stacked. Butted edge to edge they would
        read as one striped triangle; the gaps are what make them strata,
        and they let the ground through as the bedding plane between them,
        at roughly three parts ink to one part gap.

        Bands run the full width and are clipped to the wedge, so each one
        picks up the taper without any per-band geometry. The wedge sits
        inside the adaptive icon's 66dp safe zone, so no launcher mask cuts it.
    -->
    <group android:name="wedge">
        <clip-path android:pathData="M36,30 L80,54 L36,78 Q46,54 36,30 Z" />
        <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFF" android:pathData="M0,28 H108 V37 H0 Z" />
        <path android:fillColor="#9EFFFFFF" android:pathData="M0,40.5 H108 V47.5 H0 Z" />
        <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFF" android:pathData="M0,50.5 H108 V59.5 H0 Z" />
        <path android:fillColor="#9EFFFFFF" android:pathData="M0,63 H108 V69.5 H0 Z" />
        <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFF" android:pathData="M0,72.5 H108 V80 H0 Z" />
    </group>
</vector>
